{
  "about": "Frozen parity fixture for the vendored PathoROB APD reduction. Each case is a balanced-accuracy matrix PathoROB published, paired with the APD value PathoROB published for it. croma.apd must reproduce that value exactly. Read by tests/test_downstream_apd.py; the vendoring itself is governed by docs/adr/0011-downstream-shortcut-susceptibility-ships-in-the-library.md.",
  "rule": "Neither side of a pair may be recomputed by croma. The matrices and the expected values are both lifted from files upstream committed, so the fixture is evidence about PathoROB rather than a snapshot of what croma last did. It is hermetic on purpose -- no PathoROB checkout, no PATHOROB_ROOT, no conditional skip -- because CI is the branch that gates merges and a test that skips there guards nothing. Recapture it only as part of a deliberate re-vendor, never to make a red test green.",
  "source": {
    "project": "PathoROB",
    "url": "https://github.com/bifold-pathomics/PathoROB",
    "revision": "6583cf0b0d902c8cc032308262fa3a3befdc0687",
    "reduction": "pathorob/apd/utils.py :: compute_apd",
    "scalar_reduction": "pathorob/apd/apd.py :: np.mean(compute_apd(...)), which is how upstream turns compute_apd's per-replicate vector into the apd_id / apd_ood it publishes",
    "accuracies_from": "results/apd/<model>/<dataset>_raw.json :: {ID,OOD}_test_accuracies",
    "apd_from": "results/apd/<model>/<dataset>_summary.json :: apd_{id,ood}"
  },
  "procedure": [
    "Clone https://github.com/bifold-pathomics/PathoROB at the revision recorded above.",
    "For each case below, read the accuracy matrix from the named field of the named *_raw.json, and the expected value from the matching field of *_summary.json.",
    "Both files are committed upstream; nothing has to be re-run and no features, model weights or GPU are needed.",
    "Sanity-check the pairing with: float(np.mean(pathorob.apd.utils.compute_apd(accuracies))) == apd.",
    "Write the pairs out with json.dump so that repr() round-trips every float exactly."
  ],
